  "$comment": "Core state rules: create the Razorpay order only after explicit customer confirmation and deterministic revalidation; verify the checkout signature server-side with the order ID stored in the database whenever a browser callback is received; verify webhook signatures against the raw request body; deduplicate webhooks by x-razorpay-event-id; never fulfil from the browser callback alone; fulfil only after captured status is confirmed by a verified webhook or authenticated Razorpay API fetch. A missing browser callback must not block a legitimately captured payment confirmed through those server-side sources. A failed payment may later become authorized, so late-authorization events must be reconciled instead of discarded."
}
